My first ascension! Yay!  

I didn't cut and paste everything, so you don't get to see all the
lists of what I had and all at the outset.  It will be so much more
suspenseful this way! ;)


So, game starts, another Monk (my favorite class).  Spellbook of
healing (yay!) but no magic marker (boo!).

[Scene: Minetown.  Explvl8ish] Ooh, an expensive bag!  Must be
holding!  (I run a few tests with rocks) Yes, holding it is!  Alright!
 Now, let's just load some stuff in. . . my scrolls, my spellbooks,
some miscellaneous tools, like this Bag of Tricks I'm carrying for
some reason- BOOM!
Hrm.  It seems putting bags of tricks into bags of holding is a bad
idea.

Happily, I found another bag of holding in Sokoban.

[Scene: Minetown.  Explevel9ish] Hmm, now that I have this unicorn
horn I can test potions.  One here costs 200.  Wonder what that could
be.  We'll see if the horn has any effect.
h - a whistle called tin
Wait, the potion was a whistle?  Huh?  Whatever.  Okay, onto more
testing- Hey, where'd my unicorn horn go?!
oh.
damn polymorph potions.


Around Dlvl12, after clearing Sokoban and the Mines, I found a bones
file of one of my other promising characters (my previous highest
score was 280k, Dlvl26ish).  Off the corpse I got a magic lamp
(carried for light), plenty of water to bless, and some miscellaneous
tools (magic whistle, I think).

Even more fortunately, I found a spellbook of identify not long after.
 With a bit of practice detecting food (yep, the food still hasn't
moved) I got more skilled in Divination and I was identifying
everything =).

I started on the quest with no intention of finishing it then.  When I
stumbled across Master Kaen's lair earlier than expected, I went right
back up the stairs.  I had lost an earlier promising character who
tried to "get a feel for how hard Kaen is."  At the top with this
character, I wrote "STOP" on all 8 squares adjacent to the stairs.

[Scene: Medusa's level, explvl15] Hmm, I haven't seen any water
walking boots, lev boots, or rings of lev.  This is curious.  How do I
advance?  Oh never mind, I can just dig down!
[Scene: Three minutes later, on Medusa's island] I probably should've
considered how to get back.
Sigh.
Hey wait, I've got these potions of levitation!  And with this potion
of enlightenment, I can make potions of gain level!  And when I gain
level, I'll have teleport control and I can teleport off this stupid
island!
[Scene: 1 minute and 4 levels later] NO TELEPORT LEVEL?! Damnit.  

Fortunately, I had a wand of cold with me and the jump spell, so I
managed.

I spent a while looking for Ludios, but with no luck.  I've never seen
it, maybe I'm searching wrong.

The castle was a breeze (got in with Knock), and then I had a Wand of
Wishing.  My first ever.  6 wishes later, I had +5 boots of speed, +4
helm of brilliance, +4 robe, +2 T-shirt, +5 gauntlets of power (all
blessed, greased, and fooproof), and the Orb of Fate.  Thus armed, I
decided to take on Kaen.

I had read up on Kaen, and was going to try to hit him with my Wand of
Death before he put on the Eyes, and failing that levitate over some
lava and fill him with darts and shuriken.

So, I go down.  Well, he's not in a straight line with the stairs,
there goes the wand of death.  I slip on my ring of levitation.
Master Kaen casts a spell on you!  Your feet are frozen to the floor! 
Master Kaen hits!  Master Kaen hits!  The xorn hits! . . .
[panic]
Your amulet crumbles to dust!  You can move again!
PHEW!
I high-tailed it to the lava and spent a few moments recuperating. 
Then, when Kaen lined up, I let loose with the shuriken!
The shuriken misses!  You drift in the opposite direction.  Master
Kaen hits!  Master Kaen hits!
Aaaaaah!  Damnit, have to remember Newton's third law in the future.  
The rest of my throwing was much more careful.  It wasn't effective,
though.  Well, I'll hit him with fireballs.  Also no good.  He kept
teleporting back to the stairs for a bit, so I couldn't keep the
pressure on him.  Maybe a wand of fire.  Nope, that didn't do it. 
Wand of cold?
The lava cools and solidifies.  Master Kaen hits!  Master Kaen hits!
Damnit!  Have to remember not to cool lava in the future!

Anyhow, eventually I got the courage up to move next to land and
stethoscope Kaen and realized that he was healing faster than I was
damaging him.  So, I spent quite a while hovering there while he
futilely teleported around, recuperating my mana.  At full mana, when
speed was with me, I let fly some Fireballs.  I didn't kill him before
I ran out of mana.  It was now or never.  I approached and
stethoscoped him to find him with 80hp (out of 200).  I boldly pursued
him to the stairs and engaged him in combat.
That's when I found out that he wasn't really that scary.  With the
Orb of Fate, he barely dented me.  I dispatched him in a few hits, and
the eyes of the overworld were mine.  With the eyes on, I no longer
needed to carry a magic lamp.  So, this is when I got Archie the
Archon as my pet.

Newly equipped and accompanied, feeling confident I returned to the
castle.  To my surprise, even with the quest done, the stairs down had
not appeared!  This had me puzzled.  No stairs down.  I put on my ring
to levitate over the trap doors and checked the other side of the
level.  Still no stairs down.  What was this?  Wait a minute, trap
doors?  TRAP DOORS!  I yanked off the ring and plummeted into the
Valley of Death (with Archie in tow, miraculously).

At this point, the game got easy.  I attribute it to the Orb of Fate's
damage-halving, but whatever it was I hardly got damaged after this. 
I marched through Gehennom.

[Scene: Gehennom.  A level that looked specially laid-out. 
Explvl25ish] Hey look Archie, this Demon's got a name!  Asmodeus, huh?
 Let's say hi to him Archie; that's Demonbane you're wielding, right?
Asmodeus fell quickly.

[Scene: Gehennom.  A watery level a few deeper] Tra-la-la, here I go
beating on monsters-
Juiblex engulfs you!
Juiblex?  Eh, whatever.  Whack, whack, whack.
You kill Juiblex!
Well, shame I never saw the outside of it.

Somewhere in here Archie got eaten by a purple worm and promptly died.
 Fortunately, I found a magic lamp, and thus was born Archibald the
Archon.  Unfortunately, Archibald felt that I pushed him into a few
too many traps, and started playing for the other team.  I was so
angry with him I teleported him away to get some time to myself - and
never saw him again.

[Scene: Gehennom.  A few levels lower, in another one that's laid-out]
Maybe these demons get harder as you go.  Let's see.  Baalzebub, eh? 
And he's peaceful?  Odd. . . I'll walk up to him.  No response. 
Okaaay.  I'll chat.
[excuse the made-up messages, my memory isn't great]
"Hark mortal, I am the Demon Prince Baalzebub, and I demand tribute!"
"I demand. . . 200 GOLD PIECES!"
. . .
200 gold?  Okay buddy.  
Geez, I thought they could keep panhandlers out of the dungeon.

I had a more protracted fight with Orcus because he kept teleporting
across the map, but he never really had a chance to hurt me.  He used
up his wand, though.

I was totally unimpressed with Vlad.  You'd think with a title like
The Impaler he could put up a fight.  I think maybe he got it because
his face was imPALER than average due to lack of blood.

[Scene: Dlvl50, Explvl29] No stairs down, huh?  This better not be
like that lame castle!  No, this really does seem to be where the
Vibrating Square should be.  Well, let's get looking.
[Scene: 10 minutes later] Okay, this isn't much fun.  Hey wait, what
if the Vibrating Square is under a wall?  Okay, I have to do this
systematically!

So, I took out my pick-axe and started bashing down all the walls in
the level.  Fortunately, it wasn't far from where I started.

With the vibrating square found, I prepared my ascent.  I walked from
Dlvl50 up to Dlvl1.  On each level, I dug a direct path from stairs to
stairs, and furthermore lit it (a handy mnemonic in case of Mind
Flayer attack - at this point the only thing I'd genocided was Trolls
(with a blessed scroll)).  I dropped my gems at Dlvl1 next to the
upstairs, reread my spells, and walked back down.  I was ready.

The first parts of the Wizard's castle passed without much incident. 
Some Arch-liches cast huge create monster spells, but my ring of
conflict handled that.  Soon I was at the Wizard's doorstep.

Well, not quite doorstep.  It was too watery for that.  So I froze it
(I was much more comfortable killing Krakens when they were on ice). 
I stood on the ice, pulled out my trusty pickaxe, and steeled myself. 
I had a wand of death.  This would be easy, I told myself.

I bashed down the wall.

There he was!  I zapped the wand.  A miss! No!  This might be harder
than I thought.
Waitthe- did he just, clone himself?  Aw hell!
I zapped again.  
You kill the Wizard of Yendor!
Yay!  But who was that stepping out of the shadows?  Oh, the real one.
Zap.
You kill the Wizard of Yendor!
Alright!  I'd done it!  As I celebrated, I beat on some big undead guy
and watched the pet hell hound walk on its late master's body.
The hell hound breathes fire!  The ice melts!  You fall in the water!
[panic]
You crawl out!
PHEW!  Last time I trust ice!  I did in the undead and the dog with
special satisfaction, collected the book, and ID'd the fake amulet for
good measure.

At this point I was glad I had read spoilers, because no way would I
ever have found the vibrating square on my own, or assumed that
Rodney's amulet was a fake.

Anyhow, I went to the Vibrating Square and invoked the items without
incident.  Marched through most of the Sanctum without incident.  The
high priest put up something of a fight, but fortunately Moloch kept
trying to zap me (shock resistant, of course) and hitting his priest
in the process.  I did in the priest, grabbed the amulet, ID'd it,
named it "BONA FIDE" and set out on my ascent.

The ascent to Dlvl1 was. . . anticlimactic.  Rodney appeared a few
times, and each time I got him with a wand of death (I had been lucky
enough to find a few).  The mysterious force made me walk through
Juiblex's level and the one before it three times, but otherwise left
me alone.

At level one, I loaded up my gems, unloaded some excess, and nerved
myself for the final ascent.

In the plane of earth I death-zapped Rodney one final time.  A quick
confused-gold-detection later I found the portal and was in the plane
of air.  I donned my ring of levitation and set out.  Air elementals
hurt like little else.  They didn't hurt a *lot*; nothing got me much
under 100hp (my max hp was a measly 200), but they hurt enough.  I was
thankful every time a fog cloud or energy vortex or anything ingested
me - that was great time to sit and heal.

I made it through that after encountering more elementals than was
fair, and got to the plane of fire.  I doffed my ring of levitation. 
I realized there was lava.  I donned my ring of levitation.  The
portal was nearby, and I may not have killed anything in this plane.

The water plane was odd.  I confused-gold-detected the portal - near
the opposite corner of the map.  I waited for a while, following my
bubble.  I guess I switched bubble a few times.  While bored, I'd
whack a water elemental or whatever was nearby - they weren't
seriously damaging me despite my pitiful AC (-25).  I was lucky to
find the portal quickly.  At the last minute, I uncursed my ring of
conflict (damn titan in the air plane) and took it off.  I fortified
myself for the last level.

In the astral plane, I got a guardian angel.  Soon I put back on my
ring of conflict when I met the hordes, and I think my angel may have
turned on me.  Frankly I wasn't paying careful attention to each and
every monster.  I headed east, and encountered Pestilence among a
swarm of priests with some dragons and liches mixed in.  I waded
through the mundane monsters - I was still hardly getting hurt by
anything - and zapped Pestilence with my last wand of death when I got
the chance.  He was soon back up, but I zapped him again.

I pushed my way through to the altar. Lawful.  Damn.  I saw Pestilence
at the door out.  Damn.  Some priests killed Pestilence.  Yay!

I again forced my way through the crowds and back to where I had
entered the level.  I found an angry Angel of Chih Sung-tzu (my
guardian angel?) and paused to kill it since it was the only monster
in sight for a few turns.  It created monsters.  Then it created more
monsters.  Now surrounded by monsters several layers deep, I started
bashing.  Thankfully, with conflict they mostly took care of
themselves as I pushed my way through towards the center altar.  I saw
Death near the door and took a swing at him, but he backed off.  Not
one to question this, I continued my advance toward the altar.

And then my day was made.

"For some reason, the High Priestess of Chih Sung-tzu's presence is
known to you.  You feel aggravated at the High Priestess of Chih
Sung-tzu."
That was far from the truth - I felt indebted to the High Priestess of
Chih Sung-Tzu.  I charged to her.  Stood on the altar.  Double-checked
that both the altar and I were neutral.  Sacrificed the amulet.

YAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAY!

I had:
Most of the same gear described after the castle.  I got the shirt up
to +4.
Eyes of the Overworld.
The Blessed Orb of Fate.
All the Invocation Artifacts.
Lots of gems (10 emeralds, 2 dilithium crystals - almost every gem I
ever found).
Two amulets of Life Saving (one worn).
An Amulet of Reflection.
An Amulet of Magical Breathing.
A ring of regeneration (on right hand).
A ring of conflict (on left hand).

I had killed:
The Wizard of Yendor (5 times)
Pestilence (thrice)
Orcus
Juiblex
Asmodeus
5 arch-liches
2 master mind flayers
10 black dragons
. . .

At the end, I had still only genocided T (5 species).
Nothing was extinct.

"But you were a monk, how many conducts did you keep?" you ask.
Well, er, uh. . . I never changed form.
I wouldn't've hit with a wielded weapon except I sometimes forget I
have a pickaxe in my hands.
I was not a vegetarian - Wraiths and giants are yummy.
I used 8 wishes, 1 for an artifact.

Lizard Wizard - Monk - Human - Female - Neutral ascended to
demigoddess-hood with 206/206hp after 47000 moves for a score of 3.4
million.

Not bad for a first ascension.  Excellent for the first character to
make it to the castle.

